sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, one Swamp run, Ansible phases for idempotent Node state (rule 22). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:role:add
  %% kind: node.role_converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>has the role
  participant M as Metrics Node<br/>Prometheus
  CLI->>GW: node:role:add NODE ROLE<br/>--converge [--full]
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:add NODE ROLE --converge`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> --converge [--full] [--json]`
  %%> - `--full`: compare with no digest record, so every phase runs
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node and a role it already has; without `--converge` the same call is refused (`validation.failed`), except an `active` `ingress` role, which runs `node.role_add`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - applies the role's packages, files, units and publications again and repairs drift
  %%> - never changes an Instance, a Process, a Schedule or the assignment itself
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, claim the Node
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the same Node checks as for an add, and the role is `active`, `failed` at a `converge:` step, or `provisioning` for more than 11 minutes with no Operation holding the Node's role lock
  %%> - Node convergence, role addition or convergence, enrollment and agent rekey share one Node admission lock (`operation.target_busy`)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - an `active` role keeps its status; a `failed` or stale role is marked `provisioning` for the run
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent and the Node's phase digest record, read before the admission clears it (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#skip-a-phase-whose-input-did-not-change)
  %%> - with `--full`, or while the Node records a failed agent pin, the task holds no record
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-add
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task ID, at once
  Note over SW: Write input<br/>compare phase digests
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - after it writes every file the phases read, it computes each phase digest by the one rule of node:converge and compares it with the recorded digest
  %%> - `prerequisites`, `tools`, `node` and `firewall` skip when their digest is equal: they do not connect to the Node
  %%> - every other step and the end check always run, so the check still reads drift; Publish role sites always runs, because it can change other Nodes
  SW->>N: Require supported Ubuntu<br/>SSH argv · native assert
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install Ansible<br/>native bootstrap
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the Swamp role provides the worker's Ansible; it installs the pinned version and collections first
  end
  SW->>N: Apply prerequisites<br/>Ansible phase: prerequisites
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the role's repositories and packages, at the pins of the release
  %%> - a Node of a task VM's nested fleet reads its apt packages through the VM's package cache (`apt_proxy` in the intent, else the archive)
  opt role needs Tool Managers
    SW->>N: Set up Tool Managers<br/>native child workflow
  end
  SW->>N: Apply the role<br/>Ansible phase: node
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the role's files, units, ports and storage directory owner and mode; protected paths are refused before any host work
  %%> On a CI-only Node (`ci-runner`, CI places, no `app-dev`):
  %%> - the same phase runs the Instance container branch of `app-dev` from the same `instances` intent, with its nested part: the projects `orbit-instances` and `orbit-instances-nested`, the bridge, the ACLs, the egress proxy (on an Instance fleet Node with the fleet's proxy as its only parent), the shared folders, both images; it checks the CI Node's subordinate-ID demand first
  %%> - the intent leaves out the own-site rules, the development port redirect and the wake of frozen containers: the Node runs no Caddy
  %%> - the runner side (`orbit-ci`, `orbitci0`) stays as it is; a bridge range that overlaps it refuses `instance.host_unavailable` before any change
  %%> On a Node that offers proof places (`ci-runner`, CI places, with or without `app-dev`), other than the proof default's Node:
  %%> - the same phase trusts root's Incus client certificate of the default's Node for `orbit-instances-nested` only (`orbit-proof-seed`); the firewall phase inserts two UFW rules in front of the WireGuard member trust (allow port 8444 from that Node, deny it from any other), and only then sets the Incus listener on the WireGuard address, port 8444 (docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#the-seed-listener)
  %%> - on any other Node with `ci-runner` it removes that trust, that listener and both rules
  opt Analytics uses local storage
    SW->>N: Open Analytics storage<br/>Ansible phase: storage-firewall
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - a converge creates no Process and runs no database migration
  end
  opt swamp role
    SW->>N: Install Swamp<br/>native steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - installs the binary beside the running one, links it, then applies the identity, the serve unit and the worker units
    SW->>N: Enable renewal<br/>systemd timer
    %%> Order:
    %%> - the Ansible node phase installs the renewal program and rendered units first
    %%> - start the timer after all three permanent workers are started; renew the oldest due worker only while its two peers accept dispatches
    %%> - active dispatches finish during each drain; two workers keep accepting work
    %%> - all three workers stay running; only one worker renews per round, after its two peers are accepting
    %%> - a failed or inactive worker can reset its failure limit and start while its two peers serve
    %%> Why not in place:
    %%> - replacing the running binary breaks every dispatch, so the running serve and workers keep working until they restart
  end
  opt role needs certificates
    SW->>GW: Sign role certificates<br/>native child workflow
    %%> Why this calls the Gateway:
    %%> - certificate signing is the one call a step makes to the Gateway
  end
  opt role changes PHP pools
    SW->>N: Publish PHP pools<br/>native delta publication
  end
  SW->>N: Publish role sites<br/>Ansible phase: publication
  SW->>N: Open the firewall<br/>Ansible phase: firewall
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - adds the role's rules, each specific allow before its isolation deny and the broader peer trust rule; unrelated rules stay
  opt role changes DNS
    SW->>N: Publish private DNS<br/>native delta publication
    %%> Why last:
    %%> - a name is reachable only after the site serves and the firewall is open
  end
  opt role joins Metrics
    SW->>N: Add the exporters<br/>Ansible phase: exporters
    SW->>M: Publish Prometheus<br/>Ansible phase: prometheus
  end
  SW->>N: Check the role<br/>Ansible phase: check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the one end check: the role's services, ports, sites and rules are in place
  alt every step passes
    N-->>SW: role services ready
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the role active<br/>and the phase digests
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the assignment is `active` and an earlier failed step is cleared; a second convergence skips its unchanged phases
    %%> - the Node's digest record is the digests of this run; a failed or interrupted run leaves no record
    opt Node offers proof places
      Note over GW: Admit the seed copy<br/>instance.seed_copy
      %%> When:
      %%> - the Node offers proof places (`ci-runner`, CI places, with or without `app-dev`), is not the proof default's Node, and its recorded seed is not the default's current seed, and no seed copy is open; an open copy admits it when it ends
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the role stays active either way; until the copy passes, the Node offers no proof places (docs/reference/development-containers.md#the-seed-on-each-ci-node)
    end
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no match
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Keep the role as it was
    %%> Result:
    %%> - an `active` role stays `active`, so a role such as `gateway` is never taken out of service by a failed run
    %%> - a role that was `failed` or stale is marked `failed` again, with the new step's code
    %%> - running services keep their last valid configuration, and Caddy never reloads one that fails validation
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - finished host changes stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; the failed step and error code stay on the Operation and `doctor` shows the drift
  end
  opt run completed or failed
    SW->>SW: Remove the run folder<br/>private run files
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the intent, vault values and role configuration do not outlive the run, whatever its result
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
